Package: diagnosticSummary
Title: Diagnostic Accuracy Summaries for Binary Classifiers
Version: 0.0.2.20
Authors@R: 
  c(person(given = "Pat",
           family = "Johnson",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "Johnson.Patrick3@mayo.edu",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8365-1375")),
    person(given = "Rickey",
           family = "Carter",
           role = c("aut"),
           email = "Carter.Rickey@mayo.edu"))
Description: Summarizes the diagnostic accuracy of predicted probabilities
    against a binary reference standard. Reports sensitivity, specificity,
    predictive values, likelihood ratios, the area under the receiver
    operating characteristic (ROC) curve, and other measures with confidence
    intervals, overall, across thresholds, and by subgroup. Includes tests to
    compare models, such as DeLong et al. (1988) <doi:10.2307/2531595> for
    ROC curves, an intention-to-diagnose analysis for tests with ungradable
    results (Schuetz et al. 2012 <doi:10.1136/bmj.e6717>), and plots such as
    ROC, precision-recall, calibration, and decision curves (Vickers and Elkin
    2006 <doi:10.1177/0272989X06295361>).
